        </PublicationTypeList>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>Early warning of clinical deterioration remains challenging in intensive care units. We developed a gradient boosted decision tree trained on the first six hours of vital signs and laboratory results from 42118 admissions to predict in-hospital mortality. In temporal validation the model achieved an area under the receiver operating characteristic curve of 0.86, compared with 0.74 for the conventional early warning score. External validation in two hospitals confirmed calibration. Our results suggest that machine learning applied to routine electronic health record data can identify high risk patients several hours before clinical deterioration.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
