        <ArticleTitle Language="eng">Biomarker panels for septic shock recognition in children: a multicenter prospective study</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Pediatric septic shock is difficult to recognize early.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="METHODS">We prospectively enrolled 3,102 children across 18 emergency departments and compared a three-biomarker panel with single markers.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS">The panel improved sensitivity from 0.71 to 0.84 without loss of specificity.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS">A simple biomarker panel may support earlier recognition of pediatric septic shock.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
